                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
                  is frequently in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  (also def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EventuallyAndFrequently"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  is called a
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
                  of the net.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Beware that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+points"} limit points
              of nets, according to def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NetsDetectHausdorff"}
              below.
          %h3#subnets Subnets
          %p
            The definition of the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-nets"} sub-nets
            of a net requires some care. The point of the definition is to ensure that prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSpacesEquivalentlyHaveConvergetSubnets"}
            below becomes true, which states that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces+equivalently+have+converging+subnet+of+every+net"} compact spaces are equivalently those for which every net has a converging subnet
          %p
            There are several different definitions of ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subnet"}> subnet
            ’ in the literature, all of which intend to generalise the concept of subsequences. We state them now in order of increasing generality. Note that it is Definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}
            which is correct in that it corresponds precisely to refinement of filters. However, the other two definitions (def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kelley"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfDefinitionsOfSubnets"}
            below) and may be easier to work with.
          #Willard.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p (Willard, 1970).
            %p
              Given a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_{\alpha})
              with index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y_{\beta})
              with an index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is a
              %strong subnet
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              if:
            %p
              We have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B \to A
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                (that is, for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in B
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi β
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi β
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_{\beta} = x_{f(\beta)}
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is monotone (that is, for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≥
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_1 \geq \beta_2 \in B
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\beta_1) \geq f(\beta_2)
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is cofinal (that is, for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in A
                there is a
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in B
                such that
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\beta) \geq \alpha
          #Kelley.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p (Kelley, 1955).
            %p
              Given a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_{\alpha})
              with index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y_{\beta})
              with an index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is a
              %strong subnet
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              if:
            %p
              We have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B \to A
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                (that is, for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in B
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi β
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi β
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_{\beta} = x_{f(\beta)}
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is strongly cofinal (that is, for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in A
                there is a
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in B
                such that, for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_1 \geq \beta \in B
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\beta_1) \geq \alpha
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Notice that the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in definitions
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}
              and
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kelley"}
              is
              %em not
              required to be an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              in general has more sub-nets than it has sub-sequences.
          #AA.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p (Smiley, 1957; Årnes &amp; Andenæs, 1972).
            %p
              Given a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_{\alpha})
              with index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y_{\beta})
              with an index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is a
              %strong subnet
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              if:
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"} eventuality filter
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EventualityFilter"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in A
              there is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in B
              such that, for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi β
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_1 \geq \beta \in B
              there is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_1 \geq \alpha \in A
              such that
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_{\beta_1} = x_{\alpha_1}
          %p The equivalence between these definitions is as follows:
          #EquivalenceOfDefinitionsOfSubnets.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Schechter96"}> Schechter, 1996
              ).
            %ol
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                is a (
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}>
                )-subnet of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                is also a (
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kelley"}>
                )-subnet of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                is a (
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kelley"}>
                )-subnet of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                is also a (
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}>
                )-subnet of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                is a (
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}>
                )-subnet of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
                such that
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
                    is equivalent to
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                    in the sense that
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
                    are (
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}>
                    )-subnets of each other, and
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
                    is a (
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}>
                    )-subnet of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            So from the perspective of definition (
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}>
            ), there are enough (
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}>
            )-subnets and (
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kelley"}>
            )-subnets, up to equivalence.
          %h3#NetsAndFilters Eventuality filters
          %p Recall that:
          #Filter.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"}> filter
                )
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F} \subset P(X)
            %p
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
              of subsets if it is closed under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              and under taking supersets.
            %p
              The filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              is called
              %em proper
              if each set in it is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
          #EventualityFilter.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"}> eventuality filter
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon D \to X
              be a net in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Net"}
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"} eventuality filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_\nu
              of the net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Filter"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %em eventually in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EventuallyAndFrequently"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℱ
                        %mi ν
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ν
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext is eventually in
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi U
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    (U \subset X) \in \mathcal{F}_\nu
                    \\right)
                    \\,\Leftrightarrow\,
                    \\left(
                    \\nu \, \text{is eventually in}\, U
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              %strong (equivalence of nets)
            %p
              Two nets are to be considered
              %strong equivalent
              if they have the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"} eventuality filter
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EventualityFilter"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AA"}
              and theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfDefinitionsOfSubnets"}
            %p
              In particular, equivalent nets define the same logical quantifiers (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#LogicOfNets"} below
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#RelationToTopology"} below
            %p (Of course, it is possible to distinguish them by using the standard logical quantifiers instead.)
          %p
            Conversely, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"} eventuality filter
            of some net:
          #FilterNet.num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              %strong (nets from filters)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \subset P(X)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
              of subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Filter"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{U \in \mathcal{F}}{\sqcup}
              of subsets in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U,x)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U \in \mathcal{F}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≥
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi V
                      %mo )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mtext regardless of
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mtext and
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    (U,x) \geq (V,y)
                    \\right)
                    \\,\Leftrightarrow\,
                    \\left(
                    U \subset V
                    \\right)
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\text{regardless of}\, x\, \text{and} \, y
            %p
              the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              is a proper filter implies that this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedSet"}
            %p
              Then the
              %em filter net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ν
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_F
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Net"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⊔
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi U
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi ℱ
                                %mi U
                                %mo )
                              %mo ⊃
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ν
                                  %mi ℱ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{U \in \mathcal{F}}{\sqcup} U
                    \\right)_{\supset}
                    \&amp;\overset{\nu_{\mathcal{F}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    X
                    \\\
                    (U,x) &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; x
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
              of subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \subset P(X)
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Filter"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filter"} eventuality filter
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EventualityFilter"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilterNet"}
          %p
            For a related notion of filternet in a set X, see
            %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/1568548/where-has-this-common-generalization-of-nets-and-filters-been-written-down"} this post
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToTopology Relation to topology
          %p We discuss that nets detect:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the topology on general topological spaces (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyDetectedByNets"}
                below),
            %li
              %p
                the continuity of functions between them (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuousFunctionsDetectedByNets"}
                below),
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
                property (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NetsDetectHausdorff"}
                below),
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compactness
                (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSpacesEquivalentlyHaveConvergetSubnets"}
                below).
          #TopologyDetectedByNets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (topology detected by nets)
            %p
              Using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              then:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \tau)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S \subset X)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (is an element of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau \subset P(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              as seen not just by sequences but by nets, in that no
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              with elements in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\backslash S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi S
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X\backslash S \hookrightarrow X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/converges"} converges
              to an element in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              In one direction, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              be open, and consider a net
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X \backslash S \subset X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is not a limiting point of the net.
            %p
              But by assumption then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              which does not contain any element of the net, and so by definition of convergence it is not a limit of this net.
            %p
              Conversely, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              be a subset that is not open. We need to show that then there exists a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X\backslash S \subset X
              that converges to a point in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x)_{\supset}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhoods"} open neighbourhoods
              of this element (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedSetOfNeighbourhods"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is not open means that there exists an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S \subset X
              such that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              intersects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choose
              elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_U \in U \cap (X \backslash S)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Nbhds
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ν
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo \
                            %mi S
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Nbhds_X(s) &amp;\overset{\nu}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \backslash S  \subset X
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\mapsto&amp; x_U
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              But by construction this net has the property that for every neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in Nbhd_X(s)
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U' \subset U
              then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_{U'} \in V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
          #ContinuousFunctionsDetectedByNets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (continuous functions detected by nets)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau_X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
              be two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              between their underlying sets is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
              precisely if for every net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} converges
              to some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+point"} limit point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ \nu
              converges to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)\in Y
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is continuous, and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              converges to some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \nu
              converges to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \in Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{f(x)} \subset Y
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\nu(j)) \in U_{f(x)}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \geq i
            %p
              But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(U_{f(x)}) \subset X
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              converges there is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu(j) \in f^{-1}(U_{f(x)})
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \geq i
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %p We give two proofs of the other direction.
            %p
              %em proof 1
            %p
              Assuming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %p
              Conversely, suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is not continuous. We need to find a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              that converges to some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \nu
              does not converge to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contrapositive"} contrapositive
              of the reverse implication, and by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              equivalent to it.)
            %p
              Now that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is not continuous means that there exists an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset Y
              such that the pre-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(U)
              is not open. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyDetectedByNets"}
              this means that there exists a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash f^{-1}(U)
              that converges to an element
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in f^{-1}(U)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \nu
              is a net in the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo \
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \backslash U
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is open. Again by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyDetectedByNets"}
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ \nu
              converges to an element in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo \
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \backslash U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \in U
            %p
              %em proof 2 (not using excluded middle)
            %p
              Assume for every net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              that converges to some limit point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ \nu
              converges to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)\in Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subset Y
              be open. It is sufficient to prove that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(V)
              is open.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              be a net with range contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash f^{-1}(V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              be a limit point of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyDetectedByNets"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∉
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\notin f^{-1}(V)
            %p
              By our assumption, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              converges to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \nu
              converges to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyDetectedByNets"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is open,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \notin V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∉
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \notin f^{-1}(V)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              It is possible to define elementary conditions on this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} convergence
              relation that characterise whether it is topological (that is whether it comes from a topology on
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              By keeping only the simple conditions, one gets the definition of a
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+space"} convergence space
          #NetsDetectHausdorff.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Hausdorff property detected by nets)
            %p
              Assuming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              precisely if no
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Net"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+points"} limit points
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is a Hausdorff space, and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              is a net in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which has limits points
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1, x_2 \in X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 = x_2
            %p
              Assume on the contrary that the two points were different,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≠
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \neq x_2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{x_1}, U_{x_2}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cap U_2 = \emptyset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1, a_2 \in A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ν
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≤
                        %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_{a_1 \leq \bullet} \in U_{x_1}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ≤
                          %mo •
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_{a_2 \leq \bullet} \in U_{x_2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_3 \in A
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1, a_2 \leq a_3
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ≤
                          %mo •
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_{a_3 \leq \bullet} \in U_{x_1} \cap U_{x_2}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+by+contradiction"} proof by contradiction
            %p
              Conversely, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is not a Hausdorff space. We need to show that then there exists a net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with two distinct limit points.
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is not Hausdorff means that there are two distinct points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1, x_2 \in X
              such that every open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              intersects every open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choose
              elements in these intersections
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x_{U_{x_1}, U_{x_2}} \in U_{x_1}, U_{x_2}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Consider the directed neighbourhood sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x_1)_{\supset}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x_2)_{\supset}
              of these two points (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedSetOfNeighbourhods"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedProductSet"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Nbhd
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊃
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Nbhd
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊃
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x_1)_{\supset} \times Nbhd_X(x_2)_{\supset}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Nbhd
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi Nbhd
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ν
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Nbhd_X(x_1) \times Nbhd_X(x_2)
                    \&amp;\overset{\nu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    X
                    \\\
                    (U_{x_1}, U_{x_2})
                    \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp;
                    x_{U_1, U_2}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              We conclude by claiming that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2
              are both limit points of this net. We show this for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2
              is directly analogous:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{x_1}
              be an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_1, V_2) \in Nbhd_X(x_1) \times Nbhd_X(x_2)
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W_1, W_2) \subset (V_1, V_2)
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_{(W_1, W_2)} \in U_{x_1}
            %p
              Take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \coloneqq U_{x_1}
              and take
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 = X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ν
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi W
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi W
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\nu_{(W_1, W_2)}
                    \&amp; \in W_1 \cap W_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \subset V_1 \cap V_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = U_{x_1} \cap X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = U_{x_1}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          #CompactSpacesEquivalentlyHaveConvergetSubnets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces+equivalently+have+converging+subnet+of+every+net"}> compact spaces are equivalently those for which every net has a converging subnet
                )
            %p
              Assuming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              precisely if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Net"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-net"} sub-net
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Willard"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} converges
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
          %p
            We break up the
            %strong proof
            into that of lemmas
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InACompactSpaceEveryNetHasAConvergentSubnet"}
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IfEveryNetHasConvergentSubnetThenSpaceIsCompact"}
          #InACompactSpaceEveryNetHasAConvergentSubnet.num_example
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (in a compact space, every net has a convergent subnet)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a convergent subnet.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              be a net. We need to show that there is a subnet which converges.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closures"} topological closures
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              of the sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              of elements of the net beyond some fixed index:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi a
                      %mo }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_a
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\nu_b  \in X \;\vert\; b \geq a
                    \\right\}
                    \\subset X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_a \subset X\}_{a \in A}
              and hence also the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Cl(S_a) \subset X\}_{a \in A}
              has the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+intersection+property"} finite intersection property
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
              %a{:href => "finite+intersection+property#CompactnessInTermsOfFiniteIntersectionProperty"} this prop.
              implies from the assumption of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              being compact that the intersection of
              %em all
              the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              is non-empty, hence that there is an element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %munder
                      %mo ∩
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in \underset{a \in A}{\cap}  Cl(S_a)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              intersects each of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \geq a
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_b \in U_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
              (def
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
            %p
              We will now produce a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-net"} sub-net
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mi ν
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B &amp;&amp; \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\nu}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              that converges to this cluster point. To this end, we first need to build the domain directed set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedProductSet"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with the directed neighbourhood set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectedSetOfNeighbourhods"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≤
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B \subset A_{\leq} \times Nbhd_X(x)_{\supset}
            %p on those pairs such that the element of the net indexed by the first component is contained in the second component:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi X
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    (a,U_x)  \,\vert \, \nu_a \in U_X
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is clear
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preordered+set"} preordered set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, U_1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_2, U_2)
              has a common upper bound
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi bd
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi bd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_{bd}, U_{bd})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              itself is directed, there is an upper bound
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_3 \geq a_1, a_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a cluster point of the net there is moreover an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi bd
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{bd} \geq a_3 \geq a_1, a_3
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi bd
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_{a_{bd}} \in U_1 \cap U_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi bd
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{bd} \coloneqq U_1 \cap U_2
              we have obtained the required pair.
            %p
              Next take the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
